n errors when Node/npm is absent or offline.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4417,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC: '...plus an end-to-end Node `BigInt` parse assertion.'","tests/e2e/conftest.py:35-36 `_have_node()` returns `shutil.which('node')`; the bpmn harness `pytest.skip(...)` when node/npm absent or npm install fails offline.","The analogous MCP test tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py asserts entirely in Python (structuredContent / text payload) and does NOT shell out to Node — so a Node-invoking assertion is a NEW external touchpoint for this surface, not inherited from the 6fe7 precedent.","Node/BigInt capability itself is standard and corroborated (docs/output-schemas.md:110 `BigInt(ticket.created_at)`), so this is a specification gap, not a capability gap."],"finding":"The AC names an 'end-to-end Node `BigInt` parse assertion' but does not state the Node-availability precondition or skip behaviour, unlike the repo's existing Node-backed e2e tier which probes `shutil.which('node')` and skips (also npm/offline) when the toolchain is absent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f77dfbd9c47c4b611","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, line: 'plus an end-to-end Node `BigInt` parse assertion'","norm_id":"n37ca73df18f1b710","priority":0.4583,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["CI or a developer machine without Node on PATH runs the CLI test tier: an unguarded Node subprocess assertion errors instead of skipping, producing a spurious failure.","Offline environment where `npm install` for any harness bundle cannot fetch dependencies."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies